---
description: CSS module and styling conventions (web only)
globs: "*.{css,module.css}"
alwaysApply: true
---

- Class names use kebab-case (`variant-fill`), never camelCase (`variantFill`)
- **Reuse existing UI components first.** Before writing a new CSS class or inline `style`, check if an existing component already provides it (e.g. `Typography` `Span`/`P`/`Text` for text styling, `tabular` prop for tabular-nums). Only create new CSS or use inline `style` when no existing component covers the case.
- CSS modules (`*.module.css`) with `className` are preferred over inline `style` props
- Only use `style` for truly dynamic values (e.g. computed positions, runtime `transform` with variable degrees)
- CSS custom properties (`var(--color-foo)`) are web-only; mobile uses theme tokens from `@ui/common/src/theme/specifications.ts`
- No `!important` — always use higher specificity or source order instead
- Steampunk/cyber-inspired styling
